From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: what the shell hides is left out of desk captures

A screen recording's toolbar shows on screen and must not show in the
recording. The shell marks it with `RestrictionTarget.fromElement`.

- The shell's restriction targets all get one id,
  `viz::domicile::kHiddenFromCaptures`, which no page can mint: the
  `SubCaptureTargetIdWebContentsHelper` gives it to `domicile://shell`
  alone. Element Capture gives a marked element a render pass with that
  `subtree_capture_id`.
- `SurfaceAggregator` notes the remapped ids of those passes. After
  aggregating, `viz::domicile::HideFromCaptures` gives each pass with
  copy requests that shows one a copy without it, and moves the requests
  there. The screen still draws the originals; display captures, screen
  casts and screenshots read the copies.
- //components/viz/service links
  //components/viz/service/display/domicile:hidden_from_captures.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on `crux`.
---
